// Title: Application Removed Via Wmic.EXE
// Sigma ID: b53317a0-8acf-4fd1-8de8-a5401e776b96
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: frack113
// Date: 2022-01-28 | Modified: 2024-07-02
// ATT&CK: execution, T1047
// Description: Detects the removal or uninstallation of an application via "Wmic.EXE".
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team/blob/f339e7da7d05f6057fdfcdd3742bfcf365fee2a9/atomics/T1047/T1047.md#atomic-test-10---application-uninstall-using-wmic
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_wmic_uninstall_application.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\WMIC.exe" or ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "wmic.exe") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "call" and ProcessCommandLine contains "uninstall")
